##" Every scheduled US domestic flight reported to the Bureau of Transportation Statistics (BTS), May–July 2026 (1.85M flights, 92 days): late arrivals (15+ minutes), cancellations and their causes, airports by size, routes, departure hours, and each aircraft followed through its day (tail number) to measure and cost delay chains. HOW TO ANSWER QUESTIONS: use the fast *_summary sources (pre-summed, same numbers as the slow row-level sources). delays_summary = on-time, cancellations, delay causes; legs_summary = airport comparisons, small airport vs hub, best hour from an airport; routes_summary and route_hours_summary = routes and the best time to fly one; chain_starts_summary = where chains reaching an airport start; chain_slots_summary = the cost of delay chains and which departures to protect. Views named as questions (departures_to_protect_first, morning_departures_to_prioritise, airports_that_start_the_most_costly_chains, delay_chain_cost_by_airline, delay_chain_cost_range, small_airport_vs_hub, best_departure_hour_from_airport, best_departure_window_by_route, airports_whose_late_starts_reach_here, what_causes_delays, least_reliable_routes, best_day_of_week) answer the common buyer questions and say who acts. Delay-chain cost is always a RANGE: conservative_cost_usd to downstream_cost_usd ($101.3M to $369.9M nationally, May-July 2026). Filter a playbook view with + { where: ... }; to shorten one, use + { order_by: ... limit: N } (a bare + { limit: N } drops the view's ordering). The sources flights, aircraft_legs, delay_chains, chain_slots and airport_sizes are SLOW, for exploring the method only.
## dataset { title="US Flights (BTS On-Time)" }

import { flights, aircraft_legs, airport_sizes, delay_chains, chain_slots, AIRLINE, ORIGIN, PERIOD, SIZE_BAND, FLIGHT_MONTH } from 'flights.malloy'
import { chain_slots_summary, delays_summary, daily_summary, legs_summary, legs_detail, routes_summary, route_hours_summary, inbound_summary, chain_starts_summary, airport_list, airline_list, month_list } from 'summaries.malloy'

// Fast summary sources first (answer from these); the row-level sources after them are slow and for exploring the method.
export { chain_slots_summary, delays_summary, daily_summary, legs_summary, legs_detail, routes_summary, route_hours_summary, inbound_summary, chain_starts_summary, airport_list, airline_list, month_list }
